 def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
     """
-    Complete hollow sprites using a reversed palette legend on the grid edge.
+    Restore broken hollow frames using a reversed color legend on the grid edge.
 
     Input structure:
-    - bg is the dominant border color of the whole grid.
-    - A 2×N or N×2 palette sits on one edge, but its first row/column lists fill colors and its second row/column lists the corresponding border colors.
-    - Some hollow sprites contain a few interior seed pixels of the eventual fill color, while the rest of that enclosed hole is still bg.
+    - bg is the dominant edge color. Several hollow rectangular sprites appear away from the edge palette.
+    - A small 2×N or N×2 legend sits on one grid edge; its outer row/column lists fill-key colors, and its inner row/column lists the border colors paired with them.
+    - Some sprites have missing border cells plus a few colored interior seed pixels.
 
     Rule:
-    - Detect the edge palette and read it as a fill->border mapping.
-    - Find enclosed regions made from bg plus any palette fill-color seeds, ignoring the palette area itself.
